# Git workflow

```
main
  → scoped feature branch / worktree
  → Builder
  → Reviewer
  → fix / re-review
  → commit
  → integration branch when multiple lanes exist
  → integration review
  → merge main
  → release gate / tag when appropriate
```

`main` stays known-good. Releases are tagged. v0.1.0 is the current baseline.

## Rules

- Parallel Builders never share a working tree. Inspect overlap before
  parallelizing. Use branches/worktrees for substantial independent tasks.
- Small changes may use one scoped branch without extra worktrees.
- No force pushes. No silent rebases of reviewed history.
- Do not delete branches or worktrees without proving they are merged or
  otherwise safe to remove.
- Do not commit `data/`, `*.sqlite3`, provider keys, or `ui-prototypes/`
  (intentionally local/untracked).
- Do not commit or push unless instructed. Lead is the commit/integration gate
  after Reviewer sign-off.

Git history, repository files, and `docs/` are the durable source of truth
between agents. Details: `docs/development-workflow.md`.
